course: dictionary
lesson: 6817
title: Word clues: oryx
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. Here, «Conservation means protecting living things and their homes so that animals on the edge can come back» tells you what conservation means, so the sentence does the work for you.
explain: An oryx is a large antelope of the deserts and dry grasslands of Africa and Arabia. It has very long, straight, pointed horns and a pale coat with dark face markings. Those clues help you picture it before you read more.
explain: Read «seen from the side its two long straight horns can look like one». The words seen from the side tell you the horns are overlapping, so one oryx can look as if it has one horn. Always ask: what does the sentence tell me that the word itself does not?
fact: An oryx is a large antelope with very long, straight, pointed horns.
fact: Oryx live in the deserts and dry grasslands of Africa and Arabia.
fact: «The Arabian oryx was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972, but zoo-bred animals were released in Oman from 1982.»
fact: Conservation helped the Arabian oryx come back: it moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2011.
fact: Some people think the oryx, seen from the side, may have helped give rise to the unicorn legend, but no one can be sure.
exercise: «The scimitar-horned oryx was extinct in the wild by 2000.» What does extinct in the wild mean? | Living in a zoo forever | Found in every desert | *No longer living in the wild | Brought to a new island
exercise: Which feature of the oryx can look like one horn when seen from the side? | Its short tail | *Its two long straight horns | Its pale coat | Its dark face markings
exercise: Where do oryx live? | Iceland and Norway | *Africa and Arabia | Australia and Canada | Europe and America
test: «Conservation means protecting living things and their homes so that animals on the edge can come back.» What does conservation mean? | *Protecting living things and their homes | Building new zoos in deserts | Hunting animals for their horns | Counting the stars at night
test: «The Arabian oryx died out in the wild and was brought back from zoo herds.» What does brought back mean here? | Moved to a new island | Sold to a farm | Forgotten by everyone | *Returned to the wild after being saved
exam: «Some people think the oryx, seen from the side with its two horns in line, may have helped give rise to the unicorn legend, but no one can be sure.» What does no one can be sure tell you? | It was written in a science book as a proven fact | It was written by a unicorn | It is definitely true | *It is an idea, not something proven
